What=E2=80=99s next for Nvidia?


Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang speaks during the Nvidia Constellation All-Employee=
 Celebration in Taipei, Taiwan, on 27 May. Photograph: Ritchie B Tongo/EPA


Huang returned to the company=E2=80=99s headquarters to a standing ovation =
Monday, according to videos posted online. But the company at the center of=
 the AI boom still faces serious, likely damaging investigations.

The US Securities and Exchange Commission is probing the company=E2=80=99s =
accounting. Nvidia has faced serious public criticism over circular financi=
ng deals in which it lends money to its own customers to buy its chips.

California=E2=80=99s attorney general has opened an investigation into Nvid=
ia=E2=80=99s alleged circumvention of US export controls by allegedly facil=
itating China=E2=80=99s purchase of advanced chips.

In addition, congressional hearings and investigations are set to begin as =
early as next week, which will see Huang grilled by US lawmakers. Democrats=
 and Republicans alike are angry about how Trump seemingly strong-armed Nvi=
dia=E2=80=99s board into bringing Huang back in from the cold. On Monday, T=
rump said there was no cause to be concerned with the national security imp=
lications of Huang=E2=80=99s affairs, and the statement by Nvidia=E2=80=99s=
 board mentioned consultation with high-level national security officials, =
signaling that members of the Trump administration had been in contact with=
 the board.

Nvidia even faces a steep uphill climb towards re-establishing its credibil=
ity with its own investors, previously the happiest people in finance. Nvid=
ia shareholders have filed a lawsuit against the company,
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
