<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Since Jensen Huang=E2=80=99s resignation f=
rom Nvidia at what seemed like the height of success, we have learned quite=
 a few damning things about the former CEO=E2=80=99s leadership at the comp=
any. Regardless of all of them, he was reinstated as the head of the chip m=
aker yesterday.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The messy details that become public after=
 a scandal often shape the perception of that saga in the media. With Huang=
, those articles were overwhelmingly negative. His reincarnation as CEO was=
 not something that close watchers were expecting. There was no drumbeat of=
 minor news stories predicting his return. It was a genuine shock after suc=
h unflattering stories pointed to his permanent exile.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Let=E2=80=99s take a stroll down memory la=
ne with the details that have emerged since Huang=E2=80=99s resignation on =
12 November:</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=A2 In addition to relationships wit=
h Alice Huang and Nvidia=E2=80=99s vice-president of healthcare Kimberly Po=
well, Huang had an affair with a second Nvidia employee who reported to him=
