olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Huang returned to the company=E2=80=99s he=
adquarters to a standing ovation Monday, according to videos posted online.=
 But the company at the center of the AI boom still faces serious, likely d=
amaging investigations.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The US Securities and Exchange Commission =
is probing the company=E2=80=99s accounting. Nvidia has faced serious publi=
c criticism over circular financing deals in which it lends money to its ow=
n customers to buy its chips.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">California=E2=80=99s attorney general has =
opened an investigation into Nvidia=E2=80=99s alleged circumvention of US e=
xport controls by allegedly facilitating China=E2=80=99s purchase of advanc=
ed chips.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In addition, congressional hearings and in=
vestigations are set to begin as early as next week, which will see Huang g=
rilled by US lawmakers. Democrats and Republicans alike are angry about how=
 Trump seemingly strong-armed Nvidia=E2=80=99s board into bringing Huang ba=
ck in from the cold. On Monday, Trump said there was no cause to be concern=
ed with the national security implications of Huang=E2=80=99s affairs, and =
the statement by Nvidia=E2=80=99s board mentioned consultation with high-le=
vel national security officials, signaling that members of the Trump admini=
stration had been in contact with the board.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Nvidia even faces a steep uphill climb tow=
ards re-establishing its credibility with its own investors, previously the=
 happiest people in finance. Nvidia shareholders have filed a lawsuit again=
st the company, <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u0=
01.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEA13-uHzzNLsl3ZqJFCJlFeiRCDciMZ=
dnAGLLNEGpkavWYdgbl5HTZnywDqrm_BQXZiH0AvyNdjjkiLupWcey0OaXQlyn4EO8QOVChgDia=
ILrIEDGs2I8dvhpj55YmKv7VFn44N2BblUefPNrrR_dgCgIkpktdeHx5TjrW0DoSVrVyLkC53kD=
p2jD7C5BpLn1Q4g-Cg7Srn8-72ul0d_ywnd8zp5evWUbpRW8El8z5lQhxlKdKrQqP8ka0v8p_aF=
2M/4w0/ZLWNW1c6Sq2qqpOMPgCqBQ/h33/h001.Rv5PQZjc9dDCqwc9DqZQig3HZrirWd9_-Hg8=
awwkyjM" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">alleging they were misled</a>. Recent re=
marks by the board seem to bolster that case: The company=E2=80=99s board c=
hair told investors last week during an earnings call, the most direct form=
 of communication between a company and its shareholders, that the board wo=
uld not reinstate Huang. That same board had named an interim CEO, started =
an internal national security probe, and begun what seemed like an earnest =
search for a permanent replacement.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">How can Nvidia regain the trust of those i=
nvestors? My colleague Nils Pratley thinks the board has been <a href=3D"ht=
tps://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZ=
Q7fIEMgszcCSneHEAaguyuXSQw_Bm0t-xqEBAViuURVspIsBxesUQ_vzJlJSsY0XyaGehWvDtUO=
B9_NmTIcKeQXFPt80h4-ZDTCir3vNHt84-seG3VVoYIKOgknmBDoCVnv5qQ5uHZ6Ch2lgy7sznz=
9Q9bVGBalNb62Nk7Pa4IM3Q6k7SxHoc9R4D3o__Q4ukRT8pTsgW1FeiK-LneWl7qgSM0frYLNEN=
B5m7S7JOQH9mM0RXuWqDubFa_jXhi6IOM4qwSec6lea1OLDoMfuCo7BKLArcgAPHkQVo7/4w0/Z=
LWNW1c6Sq2qqpOMPgCqBQ/h34/h001.UJccoeRTgRoCdskRAThMDQVY1VyljzXWMeiOGhLBscU"=
 style=3D"color: #0077B6;">humiliated beyond repair</a> and that the direct=
ors should resign.</p>
