<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Jensen Huang isn=E2=80=99t the only Silico=
n Valley tycoon starting a new chapter. Elon Musk, Palantir=E2=80=99s Alex =
Karp, and others in Silicon Valley are turning a new leaf politically.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The wisdom among company founders goes tha=
t if your product finds no fit in the market, you pivot your company to som=
ething else. Try again. Iterate.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Many of Silicon Valley=E2=80=99s leaders t=
reat their politics in much the same way. Strike an alliance, milk it, iter=
ate, pivot.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A significant number of the tech barons we=
re major boosters of Barack Obama=E2=80=99s vision for a liberal global ord=
er. Then, after the radicalizing events of Trump=E2=80=99s first election, =
a worldwide backlash against social media, and the Covid-19 pandemic, they =
appeared front row at Trump=E2=80=99s inauguration, looking for all the wor=
ld like loyal Republican acolytes.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Two years later, Silicon Valley=E2=80=99s =
tycoons are feeling blue. They=E2=80=99re making ham-fisted attempts to rec=
oncile with the same Democrats they so recently rejected.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Will it work? There is a moral dimension t=
o politics. Treating beliefs like app features reads as cynical. A machiave=
llian perception of tech=E2=80=99s richest barons is one of the major reaso=
ns they suffered a significant repudiation in the US midterms several weeks=
 ago. But these mercurial CEOs are vital players in the US economy and nati=
onal security, however much voters may dislike them personally. Democrats a=
s well as Republicans need Silicon Valley=E2=80=99s companies to grow.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">For more on the pivot, read my <a href=3D"=
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
